@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   Every product using is written with global::. The component lives in ExPivot.Components, where a
   plain "ExPivot.Engine" could be looked up against the ExPivot component class first, and a plain
   "ExGrid.X" against sibling types (the CS0426 trap in AGENTS.md). The Web namespace makes @on...
   handlers compile as event handlers rather than as plain HTML attributes. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::ExGrid
@using global::ExGrid.Cells
@using global::ExGrid.Chrome
@using global::ExGrid.Columns
@using global::ExGrid.Components
@using global::ExGrid.Rows
@using global::ExGrid.Selection
@using global::ExPivot.Chrome
@using global::ExPivot.Engine
@* Not the contract (ADR-0201): ExPivot renders this as Show Details' tabs when the Pivot Chrome
   draws none, and no Consumer places it. It is public only because Razor makes every component
   public, is hidden from a Consumer's editor, and may change in any version. *@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
@* The built-in tabs at the report's foot (ADR-0059), where Excel's sheet tabs are: the report's
   own, then one per Show Details, titled by its cell, each with a close button. A tab's button
   takes DOM focus when ExPivot asks: when Show Details has just opened it, and when the tab
   holding the keyboard closed. *@
<div class="ex-pivot-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="@Context.Title">
    @Tab(Context.Report)
    @foreach (var tab in Context.Tabs)
    {
        @Tab(tab)
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The tabs and whom to call back (ADR-0059).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public PivotDetailsTabsContext Context { get; set; } = default!;

    private RenderFragment Tab(PivotDetailsTab tab) => @<div @key="tab.Id" class="@(tab.IsSelected ? "ex-pivot-tab ex-pivot-tab-selected" : "ex-pivot-tab")">
        <PivotFocusButton Class="ex-pivot-tab-button" OnClick="tab.Select" FocusRequest="tab.FocusRequest" TakeKeyboard="Context.TakeKeyboard"
                          role="tab" id="@tab.Id" aria-selected="@(tab.IsSelected ? "true" : "false")"
                          aria-controls="@(tab.Close is null ? null : tab.Id + "-panel")">@tab.Title</PivotFocusButton>
        @if (tab.Close is { } close)
        {
            <button type="button" class="ex-pivot-tab-close" aria-label="@tab.CloseLabel" title="@tab.CloseLabel" @onclick="close">×</button>
        }
    </div>;
}
